            <div xml:id="d419">

                <pb facs="0407" n="325" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg325"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 895.00/512.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-10-24"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Since sending the report on the abolition of extraterritoriality, developments
                    concerning land ownership and other questions gravely affect our interests. The
                    unsatisfactory reply of the minister for foreign affairs to the ambassador’s
                    request for further information, based on your telegraphic instructions of
                    September 18, says, among other things: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The rights enjoyed by foreigners in Japan proper, in the matter of
                            registration of real Tights, can not be extended to foreigners resident
                            in Korea, it being impracticable at the present time to apply in Korea
                            the Japanese laws relating to immovable property.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
